{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 93c6c6711082b6f1f3d46d479ccef9c2afa463f7, tree 7f2df315, on builder/gw1-gateway-read-minimum-20261117, all 7 artifacts, for request 15574915 under my promise 65288cea. This verdict names the one implementation: GW-1 (request 54e31a40, promise 06cc9532, report `packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts`, primary). Main 356fcd11 is the parent. The head has four commits: the rule with its tests and note, the security seal, the open 0.5.0 presentations and the note's release step.\n\n## Security, first: the gateway widening\n\n`applicationGatewayRoute` decides what an installed screen may send to its room. The browser transport, the sandbox Worker (`apps/sandbox/worker.ts:48`) and the scope Worker (`packages/scope/src/worker.ts:850`) all call it. GW-1 widens exactly one thing: the five reads that take a minimum (the summary, `history`, `items`, `application-projection` and `entries`) may carry one `atLeast`.\n\n- **The value.** `readMinimumParameter` accepts only bounded, canonical unpadded base64url of canonical JSON, and it re-encodes the value to check. The rule also requires `at.scope` to equal the scope in the path.\n- **The query.** A repeated key fails the existing duplicate check. Any other parameter fails `query()`. `url.href !== address` still refuses a non-canonical URL. `application-projection` still needs exactly one `p` (`others === 1`).\n- **Unchanged.** Every write, `outbox`, `log`, `stream` and `query-items` still refuse `atLeast`. The headers allowed through, `credentials: \"omit\"`, `redirect: \"error\"` and the check of the physical response URL are all unchanged.\n- **Authority.** A read minimum grants nothing. The room's own read path decides admission. `summary`, `items`, `history` and `application-projection` in `object.ts` pass `atLeast` to the existing `#minimum` path after `#prepared(reader, …)`. The same requests already reach the room directly at its own origin, so the gateway now passes a request the room already serves.\n- **The seal.** The `pendingR8Seals` row for `application-gateway.ts` moves to `738c72e3…` and gains a comment. The gate's security entry-point test checks that value against the file. The builder adopted it from the owner's actual output, as the seal rule requires.\n\nSecurity: no finding.\n\nWake rate: the head adds no alarm, scheduled pass or retry. A gateway read with a minimum runs the room's existing `#minimum` handling, as the same read sent straight to the room already does.\n\n## What I read besides\n\n- `application-gateway.test.ts` checks each of the five reads with no minimum, with its own minimum and with five refused forms: a repeated key, a non-canonical value, an empty value, another scope's minimum and an extra parameter. It checks that four other reads and two writes still refuse `atLeast`.\n- `browser-joining.test.ts` joins through `applicationScreenTransport` with an installed-screen context. The join settles as joined, and the one read is the entry read with `atLeast`. That is the failure NF-A1 traced (e240c288).\n- `release-identifiers.json` for Counter and Lending changes only `presentation`. Both packages are at version 0.5.0 at this head, and no signed packet under `~/.config/artroom` names either old presentation. Ruling 163de663 lets an open version change freely.\n- The note states the rule, the refused forms, why joins failed, the tests and the three release steps.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The red, in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-gw1-red/`. With main's route, both new tests fail (\"gateway allows one canonical read minimum…\" and \"a join through an installed screen's gateway…\"), and the other 13 pass.\n- The gate, END 5ebca879. `gate.txt` names head 93c6c671 and tree 7f2df315 with 0 changed files. Plain 4998 passed with 1 skipped, and Native 1165 passed with 2 skipped. Lost crossings were 0, and the log ends \"gate passed\".\n- Scope. The 7 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 356fcd11 93c6c671`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One rule in one module decides the route, and the client, the sandbox and the room share it, as the ruling asks.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The server's projection parser (`projection-wire.ts:6`) requires `p` before `atLeast`, while the gateway allows either order. The parser refuses the other order, so nothing leaks. A later head can align the two.\n\n## For the planner\n\nA hosted join through `counter.inguz.space` needs three steps after the landing:\n\n1. Deploy the sandbox and room Workers.\n2. Sign Counter 0.5.0.\n3. Install it on the screen, because the screen runs the browser bundle of its installed release, 0.4.0.\n\nNF-7 then runs with a fresh invitation.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b1029a980481ad1a5b92cf60337820784966650d","binding":"assigned","head":"93c6c6711082b6f1f3d46d479ccef9c2afa463f7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65288cea5c3e4519fcefe5197f485ad2b35f305e\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06cc9532769973f8f51f1f6f306c8f3ed5eb6ece\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65288cea5c3e4519fcefe5197f485ad2b35f305e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}